    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d429">

                <pb facs="0674" n="562" sameAs="frus:frus1907p1/pg562"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 4001/19.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Archbishop Nuttall to President Roosevelt</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Kingston, Jamaica</hi></placeName>,<lb/><date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1907-01-21"><hi rendition="#italic">January 21,
                        1907</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>We all appreciate deeply American sympathy in our distress and the prompt visit
                    of your men-of-war for our succor. Happily supply <pb facs="0675" n="563"
                        xml:id="pg563"/> of food available for relief committee is sufficient. After
                    meeting cost of this our next great want will be the means for making small
                    houses habitable. All our people are behaving splendidly.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Archbishop Nuttall</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Chairman of Relief Committee.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
